<title>CANADA: Merck Canada unit gets hepatitis drug okay.</title>
<headline>Merck Canada unit gets hepatitis drug okay.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merck and Co Inc unit Merck Frosst Canada Inc said on Wednesday that VAQTA, a new vaccine for the prevention of hepatitis A, had been approved for use by the Health Protection Branch (HPB) of Health Canada.</p>
<p>It said VAQTA was the first and only hepatitis A vaccine in Canada recommended for preventing the disease in both children and adults. In North America the highest incidence of hepatitis A is in children, with nearly 30 percent of reported cases occurring in individuals younger than 15, it said.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100</p>
</text>
